        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T08:59:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t do what you think it does. After this, isDefaultNetwork called on a random thread can return false. Java spec 17.5\n\nThe only way you can do this correctly is to have a write barrier at the end of the constructor and a read barrier before reading it. You can achieve this here by moving this assignment in the constructor, locked by mActiveIdleTimers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11050,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 11050,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "b3f3c57d4b33acd647f1e860844a47ddc887c40f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc1e8216_847e990d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 11089,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T08:59:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is written unlocked and therefore isDefaultNetworkActive is under no obligation to observe this write.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11089,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 11089,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "b3f3c57d4b33acd647f1e860844a47ddc887c40f",
